data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — wagmi@3.7.6\n_human-validated 2026-08-07 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/wagmi/wallet-connector.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-07, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test\n- chains exercised: base-sepolia\n- on-chain:\n  - txHash: `0x5a1e17cfc1df51b97277256caf90974c708a45ba00465b757f468e748e74d032`\n- gas: see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition.\n\n# Recipe: wagmi :: wallet-connector\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-07 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 17/17 automated including a real Base Sepolia transaction (21000 gas @ 6000000 wei) · 33 quotes · 14/14 offline · checklist 4 PASS + 1 COVERED-AND-FAILED-EXTERNAL. Commit 2fd4f78. (Bookkeeping repair 2026-08-12: the fields and the stamp commit below were always the record; this banner had not been flipped. No new validation — session log.)\nproject_id: \"wagmi\"        # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major (ruling 2, 2026-08-06)\nversion_major: 3           # the coexisting-majors key. PK is (project_id, version_major, recipe_type)\nversion: \"3.7.6\"           # the exact pin this recipe was authored against\ntype: \"wallet-connector\"\n\n# chains on which this recipe has been CONCRETELY TESTED (05- §2.2). Not the target list.\n# What the 2026-08-07 run actually reached. Target chains per worklist item #1 are ethereum,\n# base and arbitrum; group A reads from base, nothing writes to any of the three, and writing\n# them here would claim a validation that did not happen. See sources.json → rejected → R2.\nchains:\n  - base-sepolia\n\n# ── deployments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EMPTY BY FACT, not by omission. wagmi is a client-side TypeScript library; this recipe\n# deploys and calls no contract of its own. There is no address to list, and inventing one\n# would violate the first rule of this repo. Do not fill this field for this recipe.\ndeployments: {}\n\n# ── working_example ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Assembled from wagmi's own documented snippets at the pinned commit. Each block names the\n# evidence id for the shape it follows; the chain list is a recipe decision (worklist item #1),\n# stated as one rather than presented as quoted.\nworking_example:\n  code: |\n    // ── config.ts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // shape: site/shared/connectors/metaMask.md §Usage  [E15]\n    // chain list is this recipe's choice (worklist #1), not upstream's (mainnet/sepolia)\n    import { createConfig, http } from 'wagmi'\n    import { arbitrum, base, mainnet } from 'wagmi/chains'\n    import { metaMask } from 'wagmi/connectors'\n\n    export const config = createConfig({\n      chains: [mainnet, base, arbitrum],\n      connectors: [metaMask()],\n      transports: {\n        [mainnet.id]: http(),\n        [base.id]: http(),\n        [arbitrum.id]: http(),\n      },\n    })\n\n    // strong types across React context — site/react/getting-started.md §TypeScript Tip\n    declare module 'wagmi' {\n      interface Register {\n        config: typeof config\n      }\n    }\n\n    // ── app.tsx ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // shape: site/snippets/react/app.tsx  [E16]\n    import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n    import { WagmiProvider } from 'wagmi'\n    import { config } from './config'\n    import { Connect } from './connect'\n\n    const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\n    export function App() {\n      return (\n        <WagmiProvider config={config}>\n          <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n            <Connect />\n          </QueryClientProvider>\n        </WagmiProvider>\n      )\n    }\n\n    // ── connect.tsx ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // v3 call shape: hold the hook result whole, call .mutate on it.  [E17][E11]\n    // v3 hook names: useConnection (not useAccount), useConnectors (not\n    // useConnect().connectors).  [E9][E13]\n    import { useConnect, useConnection, useConnectors, useDisconnect } from 'wagmi'\n\n    export function Connect() {\n      const connection = useConnection()\n      const connectors = useConnectors()\n      const connect = useConnect()\n      const disconnect = useDisconnect()\n\n      if (connection.status === 'connected')\n        return (\n          <div>\n            <span>{connection.address}</span>\n            <button onClick={() => disconnect.mutate()}>Disconnect</button>\n          </div>\n        )\n\n      return (\n        <>\n          {connectors.map((connector) => (\n            <button\n              key={connector.uid}\n              disabled={connect.isPending}\n              onClick={() => connect.mutate({ connector })}\n            >\n              {connector.name}\n            </button>\n          ))}\n          {connect.error && <div role=\"alert\">{connect.error.message}</div>}\n        </>\n      )\n    }\n  source_protocol: \"wagmi\"\n  source_url: \"https://wagmi.sh/react/api/connectors/metaMask\"\n\n# ── interface ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# LANGUAGE-TAGGED (ruling 1, 2026-08-06). `05-` §2.1 defines this field as \"a copy-pasteable\n# Solidity interface block\"; wagmi has no Solidity surface, and labelling TypeScript with\n# Solidity vocabulary is what D15 forbids. The approved shape names the language explicitly\n# instead of implying it from the field name.\n# Authored against the departure until the main repo absorbs it — SCHEMA-DEPARTURES.md §1.\n#\n# The integration surface an agent must not hallucinate. Every signature is verbatim from\n# wevm/wagmi @ e1994e2e (see evidence ids).\ninterface:\n  lang: \"typescript\"\n  body: |\n    // ── connector factory ── packages/connectors/src/metaMask.ts  [E18]\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 39486 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:wagmi@3.7.6::wallet-connector::body@5330\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://wagmi.sh/react/api/connectors/metaMask\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/react/CHANGELOG.md#L268-L277\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/react/CHANGELOG.md#L528-L534\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/site/shared/migrate-from-v2-to-v3.md#L9-L11\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/connectors/src/metaMask.ts#L322-L336\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/react/package.json#L89-L94\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/site/react/guides/migrate-from-v2-to-v3.md#L48-L61\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/site/react/guides/migrate-from-v2-to-v3.md#L87-L98\n- https://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/core/src/createConfig.ts#L46-L55\n- https://github.com/MetaMask/connect-monorepo/pull/343\n- https://github.com/MetaMask/connect-monorepo/issues/342\n- https://github.com/MetaMask/mobile-wallet-protocol/issues/85\n\n---\n\n### wagmi@3::playgrounds.vite-react.src.App::Cuer\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/playgrounds/vite-react/src/App.tsx#L1-L76\n\n```\nimport { Cuer } from 'cuer'\nimport { type FormEvent, useState } from 'react'\nimport { formatEther, type Hex, parseAbi, parseEther, stringify } from 'viem'\n```\n\n### wagmi@3::packages.react.src.tempo.Connectors.test::createTempoWalletDialog\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/react/src/tempo/Connectors.test.ts#L51-L121\n\n```\nfunction createTempoWalletDialog(\n  address: `0x${string}`,\n  onConnectRequest?: () => void,\n```\n\n### wagmi@3::playgrounds.next.src.app.page::FormEvent\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/playgrounds/next/src/app/page.tsx#L1-L32\n\n```\n'use client'\n\nimport type { FormEvent } from 'react'\n```\n\n### wagmi@3::playgrounds.solid-start.src.app::QueryClient\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/playgrounds/solid-start/src/app.tsx#L1-L55\n\n```\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\nimport {\n```\n\n### wagmi@3::playgrounds.tanstack-start.src.routes.index::ClientOnly\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/playgrounds/tanstack-start/src/routes/index.tsx#L1-L59\n\n```\nimport { ClientOnly, createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { getRequestHeader } from '@tanstack/react-start/server'\nimport type { FormEvent } from 'react'\n```\n\n### wagmi@3::packages.core.src.actions.watchContractEvent.test::abi\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/core/src/actions/watchContractEvent.test.ts#L1-L40\n\n```\nimport {\n  abi,\n```\n\n### wagmi@3::packages.react.src.tempo.Connectors.test::createConfig\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/react/src/tempo/Connectors.test.ts#L1-L49\n\n```\nimport { createConfig, createStorage } from '@wagmi/core'\nimport { tempoWallet, webAuthn } from '@wagmi/core/tempo'\nimport {\n```\n\n### 3d2ec9ed-901e-5950-b0fe-aa5a1f400d8e\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/site/shared/faq.md#L7-L17\n\n```\nHow do I support the project?\nWagmi is an open source software project and free to use. If you enjoy using Wagmi or would like to support Wagmi development, you can:\n\n- [Become a sponsor on GitHub](https://github.com/sponsors/wevm)\n- Send us crypto\n  - Mainnet:…\n```\n\n### 0d8c9dc9-ece5-505a-8be8-841b46e14a1d\n`wagmi@2` · repo:d26063717aaf138e7a6f3d8ed7e606d9c59418b0 · as_of 2025-08-29T20:59:53Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/d26063717aaf138e7a6f3d8ed7e606d9c59418b0/site/shared/faq.md#L53-L63\n\n```\nHow do I support the project?\nWagmi is an open source software project and free to use. If you enjoy using Wagmi or would like to support Wagmi development, you can:\n\n- [Become a sponsor on GitHub](https://github.com/sponsors/wevm)\n- Send us crypto\n  - Mainnet:…\n```\n\n### wagmi@3::packages.react.src.tempo.Connectors.test::test~2\n`wagmi@3` · repo:e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784 · as_of 2026-08-03T20:42:45Z\nhttps://github.com/wevm/wagmi/blob/e1994e2eb7eeb461c2c1e5610887e912731d5784/packages/react/src/tempo/Connectors.test.ts#L271-L320\n\n```\ntest('register + sign (create path)', async (context) => {\n      const cleanup = await setupWebAuthn()\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"wagmi","version":"3.7.6","recipe_type":"wallet-connector","last_validated":"2026-08-07","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-07","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test"],"chains_exercised":["base-sepolia"],"on_chain":[{"kind":"txHash","hash":"0x5a1e17cfc1df51b97277256caf90974c708a45ba00465b757f468e748e74d032"}],"gas":"see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition."},"body":"# Recipe: wagmi :: wallet-connector\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-07 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 17/17 automated including a real Base Sepolia transaction (21000 gas @ 6000000 wei) · 33 quotes · 14/14 offline · checklist 4 PASS + 1 COVERED-AND-FAILED-EXTERNAL. Commit 2fd4f78. (Bookkeeping repair 2026-08-12: the fields and the stamp commit below were always the record; this banner had not been flipped. No new validation — session log.)\nproject_id: \"wagmi\"        # the PUBLISHER name — never carries the major (ruling 2, 2026-08-06)\nversion_major: 3           # the coexisting-majors key. PK is (project_id, version_major, recipe_type)\nversion: \"3.7.6\"           # the exact pin this recipe was authored against\ntype: \"wallet-connector\"\n\n# chains on which this recipe has been CONCRETELY TESTED (05- §2.2). Not the target list.\n# What the 2026-08-07 run actually reached. Target chains per worklist item #1 are ethereum,\n# base and arbitrum; group A reads from base, nothing writes to any of the three, and writing\n# them here would claim a validation that did not happen. See sources.json → rejected → R2.\nchains:\n  - base-sepolia\n\n# ── deployments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EMPTY BY FACT, not by omission. wagmi is a client-side TypeScript library; this recipe\n# deploys and calls no contract of its own. There is no address to list, and inventing one\n# would violate the first rule of this repo. Do not fill this field for this recipe.\ndeployments: {}\n\n# ── working_example ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Assembled from wagmi's own documented snippets at the pinned commit. Each block names the\n# evidence id for the shape it follows; the chain list is a recipe decision (worklist item #1),\n# stated as one rather than presented as quoted.\nworking_example:\n  code: |\n    // ── config.ts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // shape: site/shared/connectors/metaMask.md §Usage  [E15]\n    // chain list is this recipe's choice (worklist #1), not upstream's (mainnet/sepolia)\n    import { createConfig, http } from 'wagmi'\n    import { arbitrum, base, mainnet } from 'wagmi/chains'\n    import { metaMask } from 'wagmi/connectors'\n\n    export const config = createConfig({\n      chains: [mainnet, base, arbitrum],\n      connectors: [metaMask()],\n      transports: {\n        [mainnet.id]: http(),\n        [base.id]: http(),\n        [arbitrum.id]: http(),\n      },\n    })\n\n    // strong types across React context — site/react/getting-started.md §TypeScript Tip\n    declare module 'wagmi' {\n      interface Register {\n        config: typeof config\n      }\n    }\n\n    // ── app.tsx ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // shape: site/snippets/react/app.tsx  [E16]\n    import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query'\n    import { WagmiProvider } from 'wagmi'\n    import { config } from './config'\n    import { Connect } from './connect'\n\n    const queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\n    export function App() {\n      return (\n        <WagmiProvider config={config}>\n          <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n            <Connect />\n          </QueryClientProvider>\n        </WagmiProvider>\n      )\n    }\n\n    // ── connect.tsx ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    // v3 call shape: hold the hook result whole, call .mutate on it.  [E17][E11]\n    // v3 hook names: useConnection (not useAccount), useConnectors (not\n    // useConnect().connectors).  [E9][E13]\n    import { useConnect, useConnection, useConnectors, useDisconnect } from 'wagmi'\n\n    export function Connect() {\n      const connection = useConnection()\n      const connectors = useConnectors()\n      const connect = useConnect()\n      const disconnect = useDisconnect()\n\n      if (connection.status === 'connected')\n        return (\n          <div>\n            <span>{connection.address}</span>\n            <button onClick={() => disconnect.mutate()}>Disconnect</button>\n          </div>\n        )\n\n      return (\n        <>\n          {connectors.map((connector) => (\n            <button\n              key={connector.uid}\n              disabled={connect.isPending}\n              onClick={() => connect.mutate({ connector })}\n            >\n              {connector.name}\n            </button>\n          ))}\n          {connect.error && <div role=\"alert\">{connect.error.message}</div>}\n        </>\n      )\n    }\n  source_protocol: \"wagmi\"\n  source_url: \"https://wagmi.sh/react/api/connectors/metaMask\"\n\n# ── interface ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# LANGUAGE-TAGGED (ruling 1, 2026-08-06). `05-` §2.1 defines this field as \"a copy-pasteable\n# Solidity interface block\"; wagmi has no Solidity surface, and labelling TypeScript with\n# Solidity vocabulary is what D15 forbids. The approved shape names the language explicitly\n# instead of implying it from the field name.\n# Authored against the departure until the main repo absorbs it — SCHEMA-DEPARTURES.md §1.\n#\n# The integration surface an agent must not hallucinate. Every signature is verbatim from\n# wevm/wagmi @ e1994e2e (see evidence ids).\ninterface:\n  lang: \"typescript\"\n  body: |\n    // ── connector factory ── packages/connectors/src/metaMask.ts  [E18]","source_path":"recipes/wagmi/wallet-con